    "script": "[Prof. Park] Hello everyone, and a very warm welcome to M090 Introductory Algebra here at Gallatin College, Montana State University! I'm Professor Eunju Park, and right beside me is our fantastic course teaching assistant, Sora.\n\n[TA Sora] Hi everyone! I am so excited to be with you this semester. Whether you are taking this class in our Bozeman classrooms or watching online from your home across Montana, I want to say right upfront: if you’ve ever felt nervous about math or had a bad experience in high school, you are in the right place!\n\n[Prof. Park] That's right, Sora. In this course, we do not view algebra as a torture device of random symbols. Algebra is simply a universal language—a powerful toolkit designed to model the world, from calculating gas mileage on a trip to Yellowstone to budgeting ski passes at Bridger Bowl.\n\n[TA Sora] Exactly! And Professor Park and I have designed every single lecture with our \"One Problem = One Slide\" rule. You will never see a cluttered slide with ten overwhelming problems. Just one idea, one equation at a time, broken down step-by-step.\n\n[Prof. Park] Whenever you feel confused, remember: Sora is here to represent your voice, ask the questions you might hesitate to ask, and highlight the exact spots where students trip up.\n\n[TA Sora] Let’s banish math anxiety together! Grab your M090 Notes Packet, open up to Section 1.0 on page 3, and let's conquer our first concept on Slide 2!"
