    "problem": "$$\\text{Board Work: Simplify into a single fraction or integer value: } \\quad \\dfrac{3}{4} - \\dfrac{5}{12}$$",
    "solution": "$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Step 1: } & \\text{Identify LCD of 4 and 12:} \\\\\n& \\text{Since 12 is a multiple of 4 } (4 \\cdot 3 = 12), \\quad \\text{LCD} = \\mathbf{12} \\\\[0.5em]\n\\text{Step 2: } & \\text{Convert only the first fraction (the second is already in 12ths):} \\\\\n& \\dfrac{3}{4} \\cdot \\dfrac{3}{3} = \\dfrac{9}{12} \\\\[0.5em]\n\\text{Step 3: } & \\text{Subtract numerators:} \\\\\n& \\dfrac{9}{12} - \\dfrac{5}{12} = \\dfrac{9 - 5}{12} = \\dfrac{4}{12} \\\\[0.5em]\n\\text{Step 4: } & \\text{Reduce to lowest terms by dividing by 4:} \\\\\n& \\dfrac{4 \\div 4}{12 \\div 4} = \\mathbf{\\dfrac{1}{3}}\n\\end{aligned}$$",
