    "instructor": "Prof. Eunju Park • TA Sora (Gallatin College MSU)",
    "problem": "$$\\text{Board Work: Simplify into a single fraction or integer value: } \\quad \\left(\\dfrac{4}{7} - \\dfrac{2}{3}\\right)^2$$",
    "solution": "$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Step 1: } & \\text{PEMDAS Rule: Simplify INSIDE parentheses first!} \\\\\n& \\text{LCD of 7 and 3 is 21:} \\\\\n& \\dfrac{4}{7} \\cdot \\dfrac{3}{3} = \\dfrac{12}{21}, \\qquad \\dfrac{2}{3} \\cdot \\dfrac{7}{7} = \\dfrac{14}{21} \\\\[0.5em]\n\\text{Step 2: } & \\text{Subtract numerators inside the group:} \\\\\n& \\dfrac{12}{21} - \\dfrac{14}{21} = \\dfrac{12 - 14}{21} = \\mathbf{-\\dfrac{2}{21}} \\\\[0.5em]\n\\text{Step 3: } & \\text{Square the resulting fraction:} \\\\\n& \\left(-\\dfrac{2}{21}\\right)^2 = \\dfrac{(-2)^2}{21^2} = \\mathbf{\\dfrac{4}{441}}\n\\end{aligned}$$",
