    "solution": "$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Method 1: } & \\text{Multiply across into a single fraction:} \\\\\n& \\dfrac{(2 \\cdot 10) \\cdot m^2 n^5}{(5 \\cdot 1) \\cdot m^3 n^3} = \\dfrac{20 m^2 n^5}{5 m^3 n^3} \\\\[0.8em]\n\\text{Method 2: } & \\text{Simplify numbers and variables separately:} \\\\\n& \\text{Coefficients: } \\dfrac{20}{5} = \\mathbf{4} \\\\\n& \\text{Variable } m: \\dfrac{m^2}{m^3} = \\dfrac{1}{m^{3-2}} = \\mathbf{\\dfrac{1}{m}} \\\\\n& \\text{Variable } n: \\dfrac{n^5}{n^3} = n^{5-3} = \\mathbf{n^2} \\\\[0.8em]\n\\text{Final Result: } & \\mathbf{\\dfrac{4n^2}{m}}\n\\end{aligned}$$",
