    "solution": "$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Step 1: } & \\text{Simplify the first parenthetical fraction:} \\\\\n& w^5 \\text{ cancels completely } \\left(\\dfrac{w^5}{w^5} = 1\\right), \\quad \\dfrac{x^6}{x^1} = x^5 \\implies \\mathbf{\\dfrac{2x^5}{3}} \\\\[0.8em]\n\\text{Step 2: } & \\text{Simplify the second parenthetical fraction:} \\\\\n& \\dfrac{x^5}{x^2} = x^3 \\implies \\mathbf{\\dfrac{7x^3 w^2}{9}} \\\\[0.8em]\n\\text{Step 3: } & \\text{Multiply the simplified fractions straight across:} \\\\\n& \\left(\\dfrac{2x^5}{3}\\right) \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{7x^3 w^2}{9}\\right) = \\dfrac{(2 \\cdot 7) \\cdot (x^{5+3}) \\cdot w^2}{3 \\cdot 9} = \\mathbf{\\dfrac{14x^8 w^2}{27}}\n\\end{aligned}$$",
