    "solution": "$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Step 1: } & \\text{Pre-cancel common numerical factor of 2 between numerator and denominator:} \\\\\n& \\text{The 2 in the first denominator and the 2 in the second numerator cancel!} \\\\[0.8em]\n\\text{Step 2: } & \\text{Move } x^{-1} \\text{ up to numerator: } x^{11} \\cdot x^1 = x^{12} \\\\\n& \\text{Multiply across numerators: } 3 \\cdot x^{12} \\cdot x^5 \\cdot y^5 \\cdot y^{12} = 3 x^{17} y^{17} \\\\[0.8em]\n\\text{Step 3: } & \\text{Multiply denominators: } 1 \\cdot y^8 \\cdot 5x = 5x y^8 \\\\[0.8em]\n\\text{Step 4: } & \\text{Simplify the combined quotient:} \\\\\n& \\text{Coefficients: } \\dfrac{3}{5} \\\\\n& \\text{Base } x: \\dfrac{x^{17}}{x^1} = x^{17-1} = \\mathbf{x^{16}} \\\\\n& \\text{Base } y: \\dfrac{y^{17}}{y^8} = y^{17-8} = \\mathbf{y^9} \\\\[0.8em]\n\\text{Final Result: } & \\mathbf{\\dfrac{3x^{16} y^9}{5}}\n\\end{aligned}$$",
