    "script": "[Prof. Park] Slide 9 concludes Lecture 15 and marks the completion of Unit 1! Let's celebrate everyone's incredible dedication across Sections 1.0 through 1.9 with Sora's 10 Core Commandments of Algebra! Here are our 10 Golden Commandments: 1.\n\n[TA Sora] Order of Operations: PEMDAS always rulesâparentheses, exponents, multiply/divide left to right, add/subtract left to right! 2. Substitution: Always wrap substituted numbers in protective parentheses to preserve signs! 3. Exponents: Product rule adds powers, quotient rule subtracts powers, negative exponents take the elevator! 4.\n\n[Prof. Park] Distributive Property: Watch minus signs in front of parenthesesâthey flip every sign inside! 5. Polynomial Multiplication: Binomial squared has a middle term! (a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2! 6. Rational Expressions: Add and subtract ONLY over a common denominator! 7.\n\n[TA Sora] Linear Equations: The balance scale ruleâisolate the variable using inverse operations! 8. Clearing Fractions: Multiply every term on both sides by the LCD to eliminate all fractions in one step! 9. Equation Classification: Conditional (one solution), Identity (all real numbers), Contradiction (no solution)! 10.\n\n[Prof. Park] Inequalities: FLIP the inequality symbol whenever you multiply or divide by a negative number! With these 10 commandments etched into your algebraic toolbox, you are 100% prepared for Unit 2: Linear Equations in Two Variables and Graphing. Congratulations on conquering Unit 1 of M090 Introductory Algebra!\n\n[TA Sora] As we close Unit 1, let's look at the incredible ground we have covered: From fractions, real numbers, and exponents in Sections 1.0 to 1.2, to polynomials and FOIL in Sections 1.3 and 1.4, to rational expressions in Section 1.5, and finally linear equations, clearing fractions, literal formulas, and inequalities in Sections 1.6 through 1.9!\n\n[Prof. Park] You have built an unshakeable mathematical foundation. In Unit 2, we will bring all of this algebra to life on the two-dimensional Cartesian plane. Thank you for your fantastic dedication, and we will see you in Unit 2!\n\n[TA Sora] Remember our classroom motto: discipline with steps yields effortless accuracy on exams!\n\n[TA Sora] Exactly! Take it line by line, check each arithmetic move, and celebrate every victory!"
